# Google Cloud IAM & Service Accounts Lab Guide

## Overview
We really enjoyed the hands-on practice with Google Cloud IAM permissions and managing access levels between different users. It was a great way to understand how security roles and service accounts work in a real environment.

## What We Learned
* Configuring project-level and resource-level IAM roles.
* Setting up and securing custom Service Accounts.
* Granting scoped access to Google Cloud Storage and Compute Engine.
#!/bin/bash

# Environment setup and bucket creation
export BUCKET_NAME="qwiklabs-gcp-01-22f3fb69472c-lab-bucket"
gcloud storage rm -r gs://$BUCKET_NAME 2>/dev/null || true
gcloud storage buckets create gs://$BUCKET_NAME --location=US

echo "Sample content" > sample.txt
gcloud storage cp sample.txt gs://$BUCKET_NAME/sample.txt
rm sample.txt

# Create VM with Service Account
gcloud compute instances create demoiam \
    --zone=us-west1-a \
    --machine-type=e2-micro \
    --image-family=debian-12 \
    --image-project=debian-cloud \
    --service-account=read-bucket-objects@qwiklabs-gcp-01-22f3fb69472c.iam.gserviceaccount.com \
    --scopes=https://www.googleapis.com/auth/devstorage.read_write
